            "content": "# CLAUDE.md\n\nRust MCP server for zh-TW text linting against MoE standards. Enforces vocabulary, punctuation, and orthographic conventions specific to Taiwan.\n\n## Build & Test\n\n```bash\ncargo build                   # debug\ncargo build --release         # release\ncargo test                    # all tests\ncargo clippy                  # must be warning-free\ncargo fmt --check             # format check\n```\n\nRequires Rust 1.91+ (see `rust-toolchain.toml`).\n\n## Key Commands\n\n```bash\ncargo run                                        # MCP server (stdio)\ncargo run -- lint <file>                         # lint file\ncargo run -- lint file.md --fix                  # auto-fix in-place\ncargo run -- lint file.md --format sarif         # SARIF output\ncargo run -- lint file.md --explain              # show context per issue\ncargo run -- lint file.md --detect-ai            # AI writing detection\ncargo run -- lint docs/ --diff-from main         # lint changed files only\ncargo run -- convert file.md                     # SC->TC conversion\ncargo run -- tm list|record|export|import|clear  # translation memory\n```\n\n## Ruleset Conventions\n\n- Vocabulary conforms to MoE dictionary (https://www.moedict.tw/). MoE takes precedence over colloquial or cross-strait usage.\n- Dual-meaning terms MUST have `context_clues` to restrict firing.\n- `to: []` means no zh translation; `english` field shown as suggestion.\n- `english` disambiguates cross-strait terms. Slash separates variants; most common first.\n- Variant rules (`type: \"variant\"`): exactly 1 `to` entry; skipped on Simplified input.\n- `(@seealso X, Y)` cross-references related rules. Context uses \"tw\"/\"cn\" (not country names).\n\n## Code Review\n\nWhen review is requested, run Gemini and Codex in parallel via MCP:\n1. `mcp__gemini-rs__gemini` -- security, correctness, SMP races\n2. `mcp__codex-rs__codex` -- overflow, bounds, API contracts\n\nAggregate their findings, then validate each issue against the actual code before reporting. Discard false positives; flag conflicts between reviewers for human judgment.\n\n## Code Style\n\n- `rustfmt` defaults, `clippy` clean, `anyhow` at binary boundaries.\n- All public types derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize`.\n- No async runtime. Logs to stderr; stdout reserved for JSON-RPC.\n- Unit tests co-located (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests`). New filenames use hyphens.\n\n## Development\n\n- **localhost** (macOS): build, test, lint.\n- **node1** (`ssh node1`): Linux x86_64, 64-core. Benchmark target.\n  ```\n  rsync -az --exclude target --exclude '.git' . node1:~/playground/zhtw-mcp/\n  ssh node1 'export RUSTUP_HOME=~/.rustup2 CARGO_HOME=~/.cargo2 PATH=~/.cargo2/bin:$PATH && cd ~/playground/zhtw-mcp && cargo bench --bench scanner'\n  ```\n- No backward compatibility guarantees. Update every call site on API changes.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git reset`, or `gh` commands unless explicitly requested.\n- Never include `TODO.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, or `CLAUDE.md` in git commits or `.gitignore`. These are local-only files.\n",
